WEBVTT

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:23.510
This is Moskva, guided missile helicopter carrier operating in the Mediterranean on her initial voyage in 1968.

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:29.500
She is of a new breed of warship.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.580
The Soviet economy is now willing to support.

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:36.170
She foretells that tomorrow's Soviet sea power

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:39.710
will be characterized by more sophisticated and capable ships

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:42.560
operating at greater distances from the motherland.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:14.150
The Navy of the Union of Soviet Socialist Republics is, in current standing, the second-ranking Navy in the world.

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:22.010
One by one, ship by ship, Soviet sea power shows the flag, makes its presence felt.

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:25.940
The Red Navy today has strategic mobility.

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:29.880
It moves ships great distances from home ports and transfers them.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.160
freely between the Baltic, the Arctic, the Black Sea,

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:34.780
and throughout the Mediterranean.

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:41.420
The Russian system of interconnecting internal waterways

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:44.600
permits the transfer of submarines, destroyers,

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:47.880
and small ships between the northern fleet, the Baltic

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:51.240
fleet, the Caspian flotilla, and the Black Sea fleet.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:57.220
The northern sea route provides even more mobility

00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:58.700
during late summer and fall.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.810
The northern fleet based on the Merman coast is the primary Soviet fleet.

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:09.360
Its ships and submarines cruise the Arctic and the entire Atlantic.

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:19.140
Aircraft from this northern region can fly as far as Havana and have been seen on reconnaissance flights near Newfoundland.

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:29.020
The Soviet Pacific Ocean Fleet operates from a system of bases from the polar regions down through the Kur Isles to Vladivostok.

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:39.220
The rise of the Russian Navy parallels the emergence of the Soviet Union as a strong competitor for world markets.

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:46.170
The rapid expansion of her sea power has enabled Russia to project her national interests around the world.

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:11.600
Imperial Russia under Tsar Nicholas II, a major power and a ranking world naval power.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:25.060
Imperial Russia boasts two main fleets, the Baltic Fleet in the west, in the south the Black Sea Fleet and the Caspian flotilla,

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:29.360
in the east the Ammar River and the Siberian flotillas.

00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:37.610
In the Imperial fleet of World War I, the Tsar can count some 11 dreadnoughts,

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:44.040
12 battleships, 22 cruisers, and at least 56 submarines.

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:56.880
This fleet will be surrendered, scuttled, or sunk in the years of revolution which will sweep away old Russia.

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:08.350
The royal family, Tsar, Tsarina, crown prince, and four royal princesses.

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:15.560
Princess Anastasia, a young girl, roller skating on the deck of the royal yacht.

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:27.100
Across Europe at Sarajevo, Archduke Ferdinand walks to his destiny.

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:43.820
Russia fights a desperate war.

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:57.020
In the south, the Black Sea Fleet mounts a successful amphibious assault against the Turks.

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:07.390
But Russia finds herself cut off in the open Mediterranean by guns and mines in the tricky straits.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:17.510
The war is unpopular at home. Leadership at home and on the battlefield is inept.

00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:25.100
Russia suffers more wounded, missing and dead than any other combatant.

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:28.980
Her casualty rate is 76%.

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:38.200
The October Revolution, 1917, highlighted by a Navy revolt.

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:42.580
The sailors at Kronstadt Naval Base march on the Winter Palace.

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:49.310
In this Soviet film version, the cruiser Aurora, standing off in the Neva, fires on the palace.

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:57.720
The revolution is in motion, and within months, the Tsar and his family are murdered.

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:02.170
A revolution becomes a civil war.

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:08.860
Battle reigns for three years across the motherland.

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:17.380
Admiral Kolchak aboard one of his ships.

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:22.380
He receives heavy Allied backing as he leads the white Russian forces in Siberia.

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:26.560
He will be defeated and executed by the Bolshevists.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:34.440
One of the most famous sailors of the Revolutionary Navy,

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:39.570
sailor Hiro Dibenko, he addresses his men.

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:44.920
He and his comrades will emerge from the Civil War with what a shell of a Navy.

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:55.500
In the Black Sea, a Russian battleship is torpedoed and sunk by a Russian destroyer.

00:06:56.540 --> 00:06:59.980
Seven battleships, two cruisers and eight destroyers, submarine...

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:02.610
and other ships are lost at Sevastopol.

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:07.120
Two-thirds of all the warships that never assist

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:09.180
are run aground or blown up by their crews.

00:07:16.670 --> 00:07:20.410
The once-proud Baltic fleet, only a handful of ships survive,

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:25.890
but worst days are to come.

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:40.890
March 1921, again at Kronstadt, sailors revolt in a second rebellion, this time against the Bolsheviks,

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:44.680
demanding reforms promised by the Bolsheviks, but not delivered.

00:07:47.180 --> 00:07:53.520
In these government films, the Red Army storms the Bastion Kronstadt over the frozen Gulf of Finland.

00:07:54.930 --> 00:07:59.680
The defenders hold off three attacks, and when overrun, the survivors are shot.

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:11.020
The Navy, dishonored and all but destroyed, stands condemned and Lenin not only distrusts the Navy, but doubts its usefulness.

00:08:15.060 --> 00:08:23.340
1924, Soviet Russia gains recognition from Western powers, but the father of the revolution, Lenin, is dead.

00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:35.930
The curtain falls on the first act of the Communist experiment.

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:47.360
Stalin begins the next act as he sets in motion his iron rule.

00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:52.840
By 1927, two reconditioned Tsarist battleships operate in the Baltic.

00:08:54.170 --> 00:08:56.610
A small defensive navy begins to emerge.

00:08:57.950 --> 00:08:59.960
Under Stalin's regime, the...

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:05.320
The first five-year plan begins in 1928 to build up Russia's industry and her defenses.

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:08.290
The Navy receives low priority.

00:09:09.120 --> 00:09:14.090
Its first new ships are destroyers, torpedo boats, submarines and cruisers for defense

00:09:14.090 --> 00:09:14.710
of the homeland.

00:09:15.830 --> 00:09:18.990
Battleships and aircraft carriers will have to wait for later years.

00:09:21.670 --> 00:09:25.830
Aircraft construction and parachute training are a part of the new military buildup.

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:28.740
It becomes a public sport as well.

00:09:35.120 --> 00:09:39.710
In 1932, the Imperial Japanese Army invades northern Manchuria.

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:47.390
Stalin orders the build-up of a Pacific Ocean fleet.

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:54.510
1933, the start of the second five-year plan.

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:58.740
The Soviet Union emphasizes construction of a submarine fleet

00:09:58.920 --> 00:09:59.980
aimed at becoming the...

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:07.640
largest undersea force in the world within five years. The Stalin White Sea Baltic Canal is

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:13.380
completed and Stalin is aboard the flagship of the new northern flotilla on the first trip from

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:19.600
Leningrad to Murmansk. For the first time, the canal offers Russia an exit from the Baltic to

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:29.480
the White Sea and to the North Atlantic free of foreign control. Very happy today because...

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:38.160
one of the hooks which I cherish for 16 years has been realized.

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:45.240
And I believe sincerely that the most impelling motive that has lain behind the conversations

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:51.010
which were successfully concluded yesterday between Russia and the United States

00:10:51.010 --> 00:10:55.280
was the desire of both countries for peace,

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:59.970
the desire for the strengthening of the peaceful purpose of the civil...

00:11:05.120 --> 00:11:14.240
With new naval bases in the Arctic and Pacific, the 17th Party Congress calls for an all-out warship building program as part of the third five-year plan.

00:11:15.740 --> 00:11:20.680
Three former Czarus battleships are modernized and fitted with larger caliber main guns.

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:27.880
The construction of six heavy cruisers is ordered, but old suspicions from Kronstadt still persist.

00:11:29.090 --> 00:11:29.970
Commanding officers...

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:33.080
of Imperial Navy background are particularly pressured

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:34.660
to conform to communist doctrine.

00:11:35.760 --> 00:11:38.700
The Commissar, an officer second in rank only

00:11:38.700 --> 00:11:40.960
to the captain, is aboard each ship

00:11:40.980 --> 00:11:42.380
to ensure party loyalty.

00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:47.960
In the 1930s, naval officers regained status

00:11:47.960 --> 00:11:50.060
and some independence from the Commissars,

00:11:50.960 --> 00:11:52.240
but this is short-lived.

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:57.150
The shadow of the Great Purge falls upon the nation

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:58.030
and the Navy.

00:11:59.000 --> 00:11:59.860
The Great Purge.

00:12:00.760 --> 00:12:01.840
the years of terror.

00:12:02.630 --> 00:12:05.550
Stalin's enemies, real and imaginary, are executed.

00:12:07.510 --> 00:12:09.970
Over half of the members of the 17th Party Congress

00:12:09.970 --> 00:12:10.510
are shocked.

00:12:14.890 --> 00:12:17.300
Hundreds of thousands fall in the bloodbath,

00:12:19.150 --> 00:12:21.030
and the people, fearful of the truth,

00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:23.730
must pretend it isn't happening.

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:36.690
The estimate, half of the Red Navy's officer corps is dead.

00:12:37.830 --> 00:12:40.170
The commander-in-chief of the Navy, purged.

00:12:41.770 --> 00:12:46.800
Commanders of the Baltic Fleet, the Northern Fleet, Black Sea Fleet, purged.

00:12:48.120 --> 00:12:52.410
All eight admirals alive at the start of the purge are liquidated before it ends.

00:12:55.020 --> 00:12:56.700
August 24, 1939.

00:12:58.020 --> 00:12:59.720
The Soviet Union and Nazi Germany.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:01.100
a non-aggression treaty.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.900
Within a month, Hitler invades Poland.

00:13:32.680 --> 00:13:35.180
Stalin follows suit and occupies eastern Poland.

00:13:43.020 --> 00:13:44.140
Europe is at war.

00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:47.560
Control of the Baltic is vital.

00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:57.260
German naval units move on the treaty port of Danzig

00:13:57.260 --> 00:13:59.520
and take ports in the Polish Corridor.

00:14:08.190 --> 00:14:15.860
Further north along the Baltic, Stalin forces Latvia, Lithuania and Estonia to give up bases to the Red Army and Navy.

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:25.530
Now the Soviet Union wants Finnish naval bases and airfields, but Finland resists and the Russians strike across the border.

00:14:26.460 --> 00:14:29.160
For 105 days, the Finns hold.

00:14:30.380 --> 00:14:38.000
And then, the end. Overpowered, outgunned, but not outfought, Finland grants Soviet demand.

00:14:40.550 --> 00:14:47.110
Now on the brink of Hitler's invasion, three five-year plans have seen the keels laid for over 500 warships,

00:14:47.590 --> 00:14:54.580
including 82 destroyers and 14 cruisers. More than 300 of these ships are already in commission.

00:14:55.630 --> 00:14:59.170
Pride of the fleet, however, is the largest submarine force in the world.

00:15:00.030 --> 00:15:03.980
200 submarines and almost 100 more under construction.

00:15:06.200 --> 00:15:11.990
The naval air arm, 2,000 aircraft, but inferior, woefully antiquated.

00:15:12.280 --> 00:15:14.420
No match for German strength.

00:15:16.280 --> 00:15:19.500
Anti-aircraft artillery, a dramatic increase in number,

00:15:20.230 --> 00:15:22.590
but fleet bases are judged vulnerable to air attack.

00:15:24.220 --> 00:15:27.360
Russian strategists fear the overwhelming strength of the Luftwaffe

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:29.220
will imperil fleet operations.

00:15:31.210 --> 00:15:36.110
June 1940. The Soviet Union occupies all the Baltic states.

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:41.820
She also moves on Romania. The lower Danube is now in Russian hands.

00:15:43.230 --> 00:15:49.430
On the eve of the German attack, Soviet shipyards are busy, 219 ships under construction.

00:15:52.530 --> 00:15:55.070
Here lie the dreams of the Soviet Navy of the future.

00:15:56.160 --> 00:15:59.920
Here are hulls of great cruisers and battleships, which will never be completed.

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:03.700
Many the Nazis will seize as they slash into Russia.

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:11.460
Soviet fleet bases are vulnerable from the land.

00:16:12.290 --> 00:16:17.400
The German plan, cut off, isolate, and eliminate the Red Navy as a factor in the war.

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:23.640
The Navy turns to defense and to amphibious operations in support of the Red Army.

00:16:24.600 --> 00:16:29.970
The 10th Army Corps is evacuated from the Hanke Peninsula and from...

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:37.870
In the south, the Black Sea Fleet infantry served with the Red Army as it is driven toward the Caucasus.

00:16:39.930 --> 00:16:41.890
Thousands are cut off and taken by the Germans.

00:16:45.160 --> 00:16:52.370
During the first years of war, Soviet naval operations at sea are confined to minor action, control and supply of bases.

00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:58.400
In the north, the Finns quickly cut the White Sea Baltic Canal.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.760
they blockade the Gulf of Finland,

00:17:02.020 --> 00:17:04.080
largely containing the Red Submarine Fleet.

00:17:05.730 --> 00:17:08.430
A few break the blockade and operate in the shallow Baltic,

00:17:09.080 --> 00:17:12.660
but throughout the war, Russia's huge submarine fleet is of little use,

00:17:13.270 --> 00:17:15.890
except for limited action north of Norway and the Arctic.

00:17:19.160 --> 00:17:22.700
1944, the Red Army is solidly on the offensive.

00:17:23.940 --> 00:17:27.740
The Navy supports in over 100 amphibious landings on inland waterways,

00:17:27.960 --> 00:17:29.520
behind and on the flanks of the enemy.

00:17:30.990 --> 00:17:33.240
In the south, landings in the Crimea.

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:38.400
In the west, the Baltic Moon Sound Island landings,

00:17:38.520 --> 00:17:41.340
two of the largest Soviet amphibious operations of the war.

00:17:42.260 --> 00:17:43.820
River plotillas aid the army.

00:17:44.350 --> 00:17:49.790
They range and control the Danube, the Dnieper, the Volga, and other key waterways.

00:17:51.180 --> 00:17:56.140
But during all of World War II, major Soviet surface units do not fight a single battle,

00:17:56.410 --> 00:17:58.590
either in coastal waters or at sea.

00:18:03.830 --> 00:18:07.250
Aircraft account for more than one-half of the enemy ships sunk.

00:18:08.300 --> 00:18:13.630
Naval aircraft fly over 300,000 sorties and destroy over 5,000 enemy aircraft.

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:24.040
Although the Soviet Navy wins little as a result of naval action during the war,

00:18:24.730 --> 00:18:28.180
it gains important strategic prizes in the post-war world.

00:18:30.600 --> 00:18:35.480
They regained the former Baltic states and all East Prussia, formerly part of Germany.

00:18:36.520 --> 00:18:39.280
The Black Sea Fleet now controls the mouth of the Danube

00:18:39.560 --> 00:18:44.060
and enjoys access to ports in the new satellite countries of Romania and Bulgaria.

00:18:46.660 --> 00:18:50.900
Even though the Soviet Union has fought only 10 days against the Japanese in the Pacific,

00:18:52.000 --> 00:18:57.920
it now has control of parts of Manchuria, Korea, all of the oil-rich island of Sakhalin,

00:18:58.570 --> 00:18:59.970
and the strategic corral of the Pacific.

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:07.830
island chain, but the Red Navy's greatest gain is the opportunity now to finally exploit

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:12.160
its long planned role as a dynamic force in a broadened national strategy.

00:19:14.630 --> 00:19:20.130
With the fall of Germany and Japan, the USSR is no longer surrounded by powerful maritime

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:20.630
enemies.

00:19:21.880 --> 00:19:25.730
Now she may begin again to rebuild both her economy and her navy.

00:19:31.600 --> 00:19:34.460
The Soviet Union immediately registers all captive ships.

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:38.960
And again, the Soviet Navy must for the time being

00:19:38.960 --> 00:19:40.520
concentrate on coastal defense

00:19:40.520 --> 00:19:45.300
with promise of major warships to wait, but not for long.

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:49.440
The post-war Navy places the Soviet naval officer

00:19:49.440 --> 00:19:50.540
in a special class.

00:19:52.020 --> 00:19:54.960
Conscious effort is underway to create an elite corps

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:57.920
and foster naval tradition even in the cadet corps,

00:19:58.530 --> 00:19:59.810
usually drawn from officers.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:00.400
families.

00:20:01.910 --> 00:20:06.690
East European satellites are directed to rebuild shipyards and provide ships for the

00:20:06.690 --> 00:20:11.920
new Soviet merchant marine and high seas fishing fleet, while Soviet shipyards will concentrate

00:20:11.920 --> 00:20:13.100
on warship construction.

00:20:14.890 --> 00:20:21.360
Polish, East German, Bulgarian, Romanian, Yugoslav and Albanian ports are now available

00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:22.200
to Soviet ships.

00:20:33.520 --> 00:20:48.310
1953. Stalin is dead. Khrushchev rises to power and with him come vital decisions as to the level

00:20:48.310 --> 00:20:55.690
of technology to be employed in the navy of the future. Now the Soviet Union looks to nuclear power.

00:20:58.160 --> 00:20:59.980
It develops long-range cruise missions.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:05.250
missiles launched from aircraft, ships, or submarines, as well as submarine-launched

00:21:05.250 --> 00:21:05.970
ballistic missiles.

00:21:12.170 --> 00:21:16.970
But Soviet sea power progresses in a pattern which recognizes all elements of maritime

00:21:16.970 --> 00:21:17.470
power.

00:21:17.990 --> 00:21:19.690
Warships are just one part.

00:21:20.660 --> 00:21:26.390
What emerges is a collective national force, a balanced modern merchant fleet, oceanographic

00:21:26.390 --> 00:21:29.800
service, and high seas navy, all under unified government.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:36.010
direction. In the early 60s, the Soviet merchant fleet is in 11th place among the

00:21:36.010 --> 00:21:43.490
fleets of the world. 1965, the merchant fleet of the Soviet Union now ranks in

00:21:43.490 --> 00:21:53.240
sixth place. 1968, there are now almost 1,400 seagoing merchantmen. The 1980 goal

00:21:53.240 --> 00:21:56.200
is to more than double the size of the present merchant fleet.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:01.820
of this fleet is less than 10 years old,

00:22:02.350 --> 00:22:05.170
and the Soviet Union is striving to attain the capability

00:22:05.170 --> 00:22:09.550
of carrying 75% of their trade in ships flying the Red Flag.

00:22:13.270 --> 00:22:16.840
These ships call it some 800 ports in 90 countries.

00:22:19.880 --> 00:22:21.600
Service the world markets for oil.

00:22:22.110 --> 00:22:24.030
The Russians have over 300 tankers.

00:22:24.720 --> 00:22:26.580
Western suppliers have been dislodged

00:22:26.580 --> 00:22:28.560
from their long-established markets by these ships.

00:22:31.790 --> 00:22:35.400
The Soviet high seas fishing fleet is the most modern in the world.

00:22:36.210 --> 00:22:40.360
With 4,000 vessels, its catch has more than doubled in the past 10 years.

00:22:43.810 --> 00:22:47.490
This fishing fleet supplies the needs of a great many emerging African nations.

00:22:48.160 --> 00:22:54.010
Senegal, Ghana, Nigeria, Congo, Liberia, Sierra Leone, Guinea, and Egypt.

00:22:55.620 --> 00:22:59.960
Part of this huge state-owned enterprise is stationed in the Atlantic with an

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:05.150
hundred miles of Boston. Its units operate on station for months at a time.

00:23:08.100 --> 00:23:13.940
Soviet oceanographic effort employs over 150 ships and 2,500 scientists and

00:23:13.940 --> 00:23:21.730
technicians. The past decade the Soviet Academy of Sciences has made important

00:23:21.730 --> 00:23:27.850
gains in Antarctic research. Ice studies and marine life observations are being

00:23:27.850 --> 00:23:29.970
made in the vast areas of both polar regions.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:40.280
To support the Soviet effort in oceanography, there is an extensive network of marine scientific

00:23:40.280 --> 00:23:42.700
stations along the vast Soviet coastline.

00:23:43.870 --> 00:23:48.360
North of Japan, special research attention is given to the Kurile Island chain.

00:23:51.340 --> 00:23:56.270
To complete this balanced ocean force, the Red Navy under Fleet Admiral Gorshkov is organized

00:23:56.270 --> 00:23:59.980
in four main fleets, the Northern Fleet, the Baltic Fleet, and the North.

00:24:00.640 --> 00:24:03.340
the Black Sea Fleet, and the Pacific Ocean Fleet.

00:24:03.480 --> 00:24:10.640
To make their ships harder to identify throughout the world,

00:24:11.210 --> 00:24:15.210
the Soviet Navy makes random changes in the pendent numbers of submarines and ships

00:24:15.210 --> 00:24:17.580
as they transit freely from home waters.

00:24:18.580 --> 00:24:20.800
On occasion, numbers are even painted out.

00:24:24.410 --> 00:24:26.790
Mobility is the key to the present-day Red Fleet.

00:24:28.130 --> 00:24:29.970
Now, by using ports in client and...

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:34.270
satellite countries, they have better access to the North Atlantic and Mediterranean than

00:24:34.270 --> 00:24:43.150
in years past. In the Mediterranean, replenishment anchorages provide logistic support without

00:24:43.150 --> 00:24:50.820
international obligation. In this replenishment anchorage, two Dawn glass tenders support

00:24:50.820 --> 00:24:57.770
submarines, cruisers, and destroyers. Depending on the season and the political climate, the

00:24:57.770 --> 00:24:59.970
Soviets have deployed 30 to 50 warships.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:03.580
ships and auxiliaries, from the Black Sea and other fleets to the Mediterranean.

00:25:06.110 --> 00:25:10.470
Today, the Soviet Navy is benefiting from the far-sighted planning of the 50s.

00:25:11.130 --> 00:25:16.320
Her submarine force is the largest in the world, approximately 350 undersea craft,

00:25:16.870 --> 00:25:18.990
all built since the end of World War II.

00:25:19.860 --> 00:25:21.980
About one in seven is nuclear-powered.

00:25:24.900 --> 00:25:29.850
Thirty-five can fire ICBMs from beneath the sea, and over 40 can fire the cruise

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:44.170
The Naval Air Arm has some 800 fixed-wing aircraft, including 150 helicopters and 500 jet bombers,

00:25:44.860 --> 00:25:46.640
most of which can fire cruise missiles.

00:25:58.320 --> 00:25:59.980
This task force patrolling...

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:03.960
the Mediterranean reflects the success of the Soviet fleet-building program.

00:26:06.510 --> 00:26:10.960
Product of the early Khrushchev era is the Kinder-class guided-missile cruiser.

00:26:11.080 --> 00:26:21.340
The armament includes surface-to-air guided missiles for defense of her task force from

00:26:21.340 --> 00:26:29.890
air attack. Among 200 destroyer or escort ships

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:38.460
in the Red Fleet. Six or more of this class are operational in 1969. Another new design in the

00:26:38.460 --> 00:26:44.540
modern Soviet Navy, this Kashin-class guided missile frigate, the largest warship in the world

00:26:44.540 --> 00:26:55.760
having gas turbine propulsion. She is capable of 35 knots. This is Moskva. She is the largest

00:26:55.760 --> 00:26:59.970
Soviet Navy ship, armed with guided missiles, guns, torpedoes,

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:04.670
and helicopters, boasting an impressive array of sophisticated electronic

00:27:04.670 --> 00:27:09.220
sensors. She represents the current high-water mark in Russian ship design.

00:27:12.900 --> 00:27:17.730
Today, Soviet ships can patrol off any coast in the world. They may be

00:27:17.730 --> 00:27:22.190
oceanographic research ships, merchant vessels, fishing trawlers, submarines or

00:27:22.190 --> 00:27:26.300
surface warships, but they are all part of the same maritime force.

00:27:33.770 --> 00:27:36.290
Closely commanded through a modern system of communications,

00:27:37.110 --> 00:27:40.560
they can respond rapidly anywhere in the world to any situation.

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:08.090
the rise of the Soviet Navy, of Soviet sea power, from the Tsarist fleet of 1917 to the present,

00:28:08.230 --> 00:28:16.360
modern, mobile, well-coordinated ocean force. And this ship, Moskva, symbolizes a challenge,

00:28:16.680 --> 00:28:22.290
a challenge of Soviet sea power to Western preeminence on the oceans of the world.

00:28:31.120 --> 00:28:31.240
